ID: vr-09
Title: Publish the first prototype with a visual-first README

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Reviewed actual screenshots/GIFs dominate the README and a source prerelease is published.
Dependencies: vr-08, vr-10

Purpose:
Make the working local prototype easy to see and obtain, following the owner's
explicit request for screenshots, GIFs, commit/push and the first release.

Tasks:
[x] Capture actual synthetic demo media without touching a user browser/runtime.
[x] Review screenshots and GIF frames; retain provenance and third-party notices.
[x] Replace the text-heavy README with a visual gallery and linked setup guide.
[ ] Verify local links/media and reconcile the book, ledger and issue/Project.
[ ] Commit/push as verified Zanark and publish/read back the exact source prerelease.

Acceptance criteria:
README is visually dominated by real screenshots and multiple animated GIFs,
not mockups. No private URL/capability, personal speech, model/native asset,
credential or continuity file enters publication. Demo uses a separate RAM
state/profile and copied numeric cache, sharing only read-only source/model
files and bounded CPU resources. No app defaults change or active runtime restart.
Release is explicitly an early source prerelease, not an installer or accuracy
acceptance; limitations and fresh-clone setup remain reachable.

Completion evidence:
Actual final vr-10 renderer captured in isolated Edge using a synthetic greeting
and the visible preferred Zira settings. Four PNGs and two silent GIFs dominate
the README; full operating/setup/limitations text preserved in linked guide.
GIFs sample the actual generated timeline (not a60fps recording); no source
reference image, personal speech, capability or downloaded asset is included.
Windows decoder confirms40/24frames; decoded samples and PNGs inspected.
Exact remote source/tag/release verification pending.

Completion log:
2026-11-19 - Owner authorizes visual README, regular commit/push and first
prototype release. Existing releases empty; PAT login verified as Zanark.
2026-11-19 - Owner's additional facial/60fps feedback implemented before final
media. Early captures retained privately, replaced in the public gallery.
